    "d5d7e7fab31058bba0fd714d5aac8ca64b564b49923d3ebfb86eb9a7fbdb32d0": {
      "normalizationVersion": 1,
      "sourceHash": "cd800c8e1902c24e12d13655e3c7195de8a11433a5d8dcf876e15ed8ef53aab4",
      "contextFingerprint": "334381918947006220c8b5c8283d156f6a6b45bd733498b9b44cda81462f819d",
      "sourceText": "通过红、绿、蓝3种颜色不同比例的混合能够让图像展现出五彩斑斓的颜色，这种模型称为RGB颜色模型。RGB颜色模型是最常见的颜色模型之一，常用于表示和显示图像。为了能够表示3种颜色的混合，图像以多通道的形式分别存储某一种颜色的红色分量、绿色分量和蓝色分量。除RGB颜色模型外，图像的颜色模型还有YUV、HSV等模型，分别表示图像的亮度、色度、饱和度等分量。了解图像颜色空间对分割拥有颜色区分特征的图像具有重要的帮助，例如提取图像中的红色物体可以通过比较图像红色通道的像素值来实现。",
      "translatedText": "By mixing the three colors red, green, and blue in different proportions, images can display a rich array of colors\\. This model is called the RGB color model\\. The RGB color model is one of the most common color models and is often used to represent and display images\\. To represent the mixture of the three colors, images store the red component, green component, and blue component of a certain color separately in a multi\\-channel format\\. In addition to the RGB color model, image color models also include YUV, HSV, and other models, which respectively represent components such as brightness, chrominance, and saturation of the image\\. Understanding image color spaces is of great help for segmenting images with color\\-distinguishing features\\. For example, extracting red objects from an image can be achieved by comparing the pixel values of the image's red channel\\.",
      "provider": "deepseek",
      "model": "deepseek-flash",
      "usage": {
        "inputTokens": 257,
        "outputTokens": 176,
        "costUsd": 0.000289
      }
    },
